.TH PRCTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
prctl \- invokes linux prctl with five fixed arguments
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/prctl.h>
.B int prctl(int option, unsigned long argument2, unsigned long argument3, unsigned long argument4, unsigned long argument5);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes Linux prctl with five fixed integer arguments. Pass zero for unused arguments.
Use
.BR prctl_ptr (3crunch)
when the second argument is a pointer.
The fixed signatures do not accept pointer arguments in positions three
through five in Crunch source.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR prctl (2)
